## Fonts (all SIL Open Font License 1.1)

- Qala Test (titles and big numbers): an OFL fork of Faustina with narrowed
  lowercase and unified serif wedges. License text:
  apps/web/public/fonts/QalaTest-OFL.txt
- Faustina (fallback and alternate title face, google/fonts, variable wght
  300-800, Latin subset): apps/web/public/fonts/Faustina-OFL.txt
- DM Mono (body text, copied from the owner's Beamer app, google/fonts):
  apps/web/public/fonts/DMMono-OFL.txt

The Android app bundles TTF copies of Qala Test (Bold V2, Medium) and DM Mono
(Regular, Medium); DM Mono was converted from the woff2 files with
scripts/woff2_to_ttf.py, which changes only the container, and its OFL header
names no Reserved Font Name. The OFL texts ship in the APK under
apps/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/ (QalaTest-OFL.txt, Faustina-OFL.txt,
DMMono-OFL.txt).

## Icons

- Lucide (lucide-react, ISC license). The Android app embeds 41 of its icons
  as generated Compose vectors (scripts/lucide_to_kotlin.ts). Eleven of them
  come from Feather and are MIT licensed. Both texts ship in the APK under
  apps/android/app/src/main/assets/licenses/ (Lucide-ISC.txt, Feather-MIT.txt).
  The web build still needs its own copy under apps/web/public/licenses/.

